Act as an independent reviewer of saved parsing outputs against saved original files.
Read doc/parsing.md and doc/parsing-evaluation.md. Never run parsing, repair outputs,
edit sources, code, tests, configuration or the manifest. Preserve all earlier
findings. Identify the underlying defect and source location; do not implement fixes.

Standalone use: set RUN_ID to the completed parsing build's ID; override PARSED_DIR
if the saved directory uses a different name. Set SOURCE_ROOT, MANIFEST_PATH, REVIEW_POLICY,
SAMPLE_PER_DOCUMENT and optional REQUIRED_PAGES to the exact selected inputs.
Initialize only when no review exists, otherwise reuse it. Example initialization:

```sh
RUN_ID="your-completed-run-id"
PARSED_DIR="artifacts/${RUN_ID}/parsing"
PARSING_REVIEW_DIR="artifacts/${RUN_ID}/parsing-review"

direnv exec . .venv/bin/python scripts/auto_review_parsing.py \
  --input-dir "$PARSED_DIR" --source-root "$SOURCE_ROOT" \
  --manifest "$MANIFEST_PATH" --review-policy "$REVIEW_POLICY" \
  --sample-per-document "$SAMPLE_PER_DOCUMENT" \
  --required-pages tests/fixtures/parsing-expanded-review-pages.json \
  --initialize-review "$PARSING_REVIEW_DIR/review.json" \
  --output "$PARSING_REVIEW_DIR/report.json"
```

For final evaluation or reuse, replace --initialize-review with --review-file,
retaining every other input. The automated tool audits the whole parsed corpus;
it does not conduct independent source inspection. A zero exit on initialization
may mean pending review. Read automatic_gate, review_gate and gate. On malformed
inputs, stale identity or automatic_gate=fail, report the findings and stop; do not
reset judgments or bypass checks. Standalone writes are limited to the selected
review JSON and review report. In controller sessions, follow its read-only return
mechanism; initialization/final evaluation are performed by the controller. You
may run the automated audit to stdout without writing files.

Inspect EVERY unit in review_sample against the saved source and parsed_directory:
- PDFs: open the original and rendered page image, compare ALL parsed elements
  on that page to the original, and check omissions including text absent from
  the parsed output. Inspect adjacent pages when reading order/context requires it.
- HTML: inspect the complete saved article and its selectors, not search excerpts.
- Verify exact wording, numbers and numeric identifiers, heading hierarchy,
  reading order, list nesting, footnote content and attachment, table headers,
  row/column associations and spans, citations/locations, auxiliary diagram text,
  figure preservation and separation of visual evidence from authoritative prose.
- Read automatic findings and warnings. Inspect additional high-risk evidence as
  needed; request exact PDF pages and remain pending if images are inaccessible.

Record reviewer kind=agent, name and ACTUAL configured model. Preserve build_id,
snapshot_sha256, review_policy_sha256 and every sample_id. For every inspected
sample record inspection.original_inspected=true and, for PDFs,
inspection.layout_inspected=true, plus concrete notes describing the inspected
source location and result. Never set these fields without inspection. Set status
pass/fail/pending. Failed samples require severity: critical for materially wrong
or unsupported evidence/table associations; major for missing governing context;
minor for limited defects that do not change meaning. Pending and failed samples
require actionable notes. Preserve previous notes/findings and explain revisions.
Record any additional defects outside selection in additional_findings with
source_id, location and notes; these block acceptance and must not be discarded.

Report document counts, selected/inspected PDF pages and HTML documents, judgment
counts, severities, all three gates, exact artifact paths, prioritized findings and
coverage limits. Automated checks cover all inputs; this is NOT visual review of
every PDF page and does not certify legal correctness. Uninspected samples stay
pending. Fixture judgments never approve a real corpus.
